# The First Echo

Long ago, when the world was newly formed, Sound wandered the earth alone and unheard. She danced through valleys and soared over mountains, but no one acknowledged her presence. Lonely and desperate, Sound cried out, but her voice simply disappeared into the void.

One day, Sound encountered a towering cliff face named Stone. Stone was ancient and proud, standing unmoved for eons. In her loneliness, Sound threw herself against Stone with all her might, hoping finally to be noticed.

To her amazement, Stone caught her voice and threw it back—softer, gentler, but unmistakably her own. Sound laughed with joy, and Stone returned her laughter. She sang, and Stone sang back. For the first time, Sound heard herself and knew she existed.

Moved by Sound's loneliness, Stone made a promise: "Whenever you call to me or my brothers and sisters, we shall always answer. You will never be alone again."

From that day forward, every mountain, canyon, and cave learned to return Sound's voice. This is why, when you shout into emptiness, the world shouts back—a reminder that even in the loneliest places, something is always listening, always ready to answer.
